# AGENTS.md

Pokémon-style gacha / merge / battle browser game with all UI text in Vietnamese.

**Policy: only develop in the Vue app (`framework/`). The legacy vanilla codebase is FROZEN — do not modify `vanilla/` anymore.** Treat `vanilla/` as read-only reference only (formulas, data, battle rules).

## The active codebase
- **Vue 3 migration** in `framework/` — Vite + Vue 3 `<script setup>` + Tailwind CSS v4.
- `framework/src/game/` holds the extracted pure logic as ES modules: `data.js`, `skills.js`, `stats.js`, `gacha.js`, `inventory.js`, `merge.js`, `shop.js`, `store.js`, `battle.js`, `campaign.js`, `gym.js`.
- `framework/src/game/store.js` exports a Vue `reactive` `store` singleton (same shape as legacy `vanilla/js/state.js`) with save/load. It reads/writes `localStorage` key `pokemonGameState`.
- UI is SFCs under `framework/src/components/` and `framework/src/views/`. Tailwind utility classes only — no custom CSS unless absolutely necessary.
- All 7 tabs render real views: Gacha (`views/GachaView.vue`, `components/gacha/*`), Roster (`views/RosterView.vue`, `components/poke/*` incl. Pokédex + detail modals), Merge (🧬 `views/MergeView.vue`, `components/merge/*`, logic in `game/merge.js` incl. talent unlock at V1/V3/V5), Shop (`views/ShopView.vue` — mua Kẹo Kinh Nghiệm), Inventory/Kho đồ (`views/InventoryView.vue`, `components/shop/*`, logic in `game/shop.js` incl. skill-select modal khi dùng Kẹo chạm mốc level chia hết cho 5), Campaign (⚔️ `views/CampaignView.vue`, logic in `game/campaign.js`) and Gym (🏟️ `views/GymView.vue`, logic in `game/gym.js`). Campaign + Gym share the reactive battle engine in `game/battle.js` and the battle UI in `components/battle/BattleArena.vue` (with `BattleTeamSelectModal.vue` for team setup).
- **World Map Navigation (Phaser 4)**: `src/game/world.js` defines WORLD_WIDTH/HEIGHT (1600×1000), LOCATIONS, OBSTACLES, and collision/interaction helpers (`getBuildingColliders`, `getLocationAt`, `isInInteractRange`). `src/components/map/WorldMap.vue` mounts a Phaser `Game` (v4.2.1, `phaser/dist/phaser.esm.js`) into a container and destroys it on unmount (`v-if` in App.vue); the map itself is rendered by `src/components/map/worldScene.js` (class `WorldScene`, communicates to Vue via module-level `setWorldRuntime({callbacks, startPos})` + scene `init(data)`). WASD/Arrow move at 220px/s with Arcade physics (player body `setSize(20,40)` offset `(6,24)`, `setCollideWorldBounds` on a physics world explicitly sized to `setBounds(0,0,WORLD_WIDTH,WORLD_HEIGHT)` — default bounds are canvas-sized and would clamp wrong). **Terrain is data-driven**: `src/game/worldmap.js` exports the 50×32 tile grid (`getMapGrid()` reads `localStorage['pokemonMapGrid']` first, else `DEFAULT_GRID`; 0 = "cỏ tự động" via `autoGrassTile`, otherwise a tile index into terrain.png). `src/components/map/MapEditor.vue` (opened via the "✏️ Sửa bản đồ" button on WorldMap) is a canvas tile painter (vẽ/tô màu/chữ nhật/tẩy, palette of all 117 tiles) that saves to localStorage and exports `DEFAULT_GRID` code for `worldmap.js`. Tilemap built from `public/images/map/terrain.png` (416×288 = 13×9 tiles @32px, upscaled 2× from the 16px source so tile indexes stay 0-based with `addTilesetImage('terrain','terrain',32,32,0,0)`). Player sprite `player_red.png` = 9 frames of 16×32 (anims `walk-down/up/left`, right = `flipX`). Camera `setBounds` + `startFollow`. Locations have interaction radius; on entry (edge-triggered with debounce 30, anti-loop via `lastInRangeLocId` init) single-mode locations fire `onOpen(mode)`, dual-mode (Nhà, Cửa hàng) fire `onShowPopover(loc)`. `store.worldPos` persists player position across sessions. Assets credited in `public/images/map/CREDITS.md` (pokeemerald red.png + Red_Voxel CC-BY-SA 3.0).

## Run & verify
- `cd framework; npm run dev` (Vite dev server). Build check: `npm run build`. No tests exist.
- The Gacha tab has a built-in cheat panel (add PokePoint/PokeGacha, set level, reset resources) — use it to test instead of editing state.
- There are no lint/test commands. Don't invent them.

## Battle rules (verbatim from legacy)
- Turn order is normal turn-based — Tốc Độ (SPD) only decides who acts first when a Pokémon just enters the field (wave start / in-battle switch), tie = random 50/50; there is NO speed gauge / `spdGauge` / speed recovery — turns strictly alternate after the first move.
- campaign DoT = `%` of current HP, gym DoT = flat `val`; campaign enemies built with `baseHp + level*25` / `baseAtk + level*5` / `baseDef + level*3` / `baseSpeed + level*2`, gym enemies use exponential `Math.pow(1+rate, level-1)` growth.
- gym requires HLV level ≥ 25 to unlock, team must be same type and level ≤ trainer level, and completed gyms (progress ≥ 5) can't be rechallenged; gym buff +10% (`gymBuffs[type] = 0.1`) at 5 cleared, then `recalculatePokemonStats` for all that type.
- Status effects: `stun` (Choáng) makes the affected Pokémon lose 1 turn; `extra_turn` (Tăng Tốc +1 lượt) grants an extra attack on entry.

## Conventions
- Never use legacy DOM helpers (`document.getElementById`, `innerHTML`, etc.) in the Vue app — use reactivity.
- Keep new UI text and comments in Vietnamese to match the codebase.
- Don't modify anything under `vanilla/` (frozen legacy).
- Branch `develop` currently has a large uncommitted refactor in progress; don't commit unless asked.

## Environment
- Windows + PowerShell 5.1: no `&&` chaining — use `cmd1; if ($?) { cmd2 }`.
- Git `core.autocrlf=true`: tree is LF; diffs may show LF→CRLF warnings, which are harmless.
